```

## Why This Is Asked

Gauges practical conflict handling, clarity in decision criteria, and discipline in following up with measurable feedback loops.

## Key Concepts

- Surface interests, separate people from problem
- Generate multiple actionable options
- Use objective criteria to decide
- Establish concrete feedback loops and ownership

## Code Example

```javascript
function scoreOption(option) {
  const criteria = { risk: 3, impact: 3, maintenance: 2, time: 2 };
  return Object.keys(criteria).reduce((acc, k) => {
    return acc + (option[k] ? criteria[k] : -criteria[k]);
  }, 0);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you document the decision so future audits understand it?
- What indicators would trigger a re-evaluation of the chosen option?

## Why This Is Asked
IBM wants to see how you handle change management, influence without authority, and drive technical decisions through data and collaboration rather than just technical expertise.

## Expected Answer
A strong candidate will describe: 1) A specific technical challenge or opportunity, 2) How they gathered data/evidence to support their proposal, 3) How they addressed team concerns through demos or proof-of-concepts, 4) The measurable business impact of the change.

